<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01LT">Remark <span data-tag="01LT">4.6.7.20</span>.</a> The adjunction of Corollary <a data-tag="01LS" href="/tag/01LS">4.6.7.19</a> has an interpretation in the framework of Proposition <a data-tag="002F" href="/tag/002F">1.2.3.15</a>. Let $Q^{\bullet }$ denote the cosimplicial object of $\operatorname{Set_{\Delta }}$ given by the construction $[n] \mapsto \Phi ( \Delta ^ n )$. For every simplicial set $B$, Corollary <a data-tag="01LR" href="/tag/01LR">4.6.7.18</a> supplies a canonical isomorphism of simplicial sets </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname{Hom}^{\mathrm{L}}_{ \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }^{\operatorname{hc}}( \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}[B] )}(x,y) \simeq \operatorname{Sing}_{\bullet }^{Q}( B ), \]
</div>
<p> where $\operatorname{Sing}_{\bullet }^{Q}(B)$ is the simplicial set defined in Variant <a data-tag="001T" href="/tag/001T">1.2.2.8</a>. It follows that $\Phi $ can be identified with the generalized geometric realization functor $K \mapsto | K |^{Q}$ of Proposition <a data-tag="002F" href="/tag/002F">1.2.3.15</a>. </p>
</article>
